WHAT'S NEW IN v4.0
──────────────────
  ① Immersive school architecture renderer
       • SchoolArchitecture class draws full hallway perspective scenes
       • Each floor zone (Floors 1-3, 4-6, 7-8, 9-10) has unique visual theme:
           Trust Zone   — warm fluorescent lights, clean lockers, posters
           Doubt Zone   — flickering lights, graffiti, peeling paint
           Paranoia Zone— broken windows, police tape, overgrown floor
           Endgame Zone — structural collapse, emergency lighting, void doors
       • Procedural locker rows, ceiling tiles, floor tiles, notice boards
       • Animated environmental details: flickering bulbs, swinging door, dust motes

  ② Per-click contextual sound system (27 distinct sounds)
       • Click sounds rotate through 6 variants keyed to UI context
       • Button hover: whisper tick (≠ click, avoids over-saturation)
       • Task buttons: heavy chalk thunk
       • Vote buttons: institutional bell fragment
       • Navigation buttons: door-creak + footstep combo
       • Success/fail audio layers added on top of base click
       • No two consecutive clicks ever play the same sound

  ③ Floor progression gate
       • GameState.floor_unlocked tracks per-floor completion status
       • FloorScene shows locked overlay if mini-task not yet completed
       • "Advance Floor" button is DISABLED and grayed with explanation
         until current floor's mini-task earns its clue bonus
       • LobbyScene shows lock icon and "Complete the floor task first" notice
       • Engine.can_advance_floor() → bool used by all transition points

  ④ Character customizer with Studs option + full integration
       • CustomizeScene: tabbed panel (Face · Hair · Outfit · Studs · Preview)
       • Studs tab: piercing placement picker (ear, nose, lip, eyebrow, septum)
         each with colour picker (gold, silver, rose-gold, black, gemstone)
       • Human player config persisted in GameState.human_config
       • SpriteFactory.draw_studs() renderer integrated into main draw pipeline
       • Accessible from lobby via "Customize" button (non-modal, returns to lobby)
       • NPC studs visible in vote/lobby screens for character variety
"""

